    "ref": "slag-atlas-1995", "figure": "Fig. 3.249", "diagram": "Liquidus surface in the CaO-MgO-SiO2 system as evaluated by Osborn, Muan", "printedPage": 134, "pdfPage": 154,
    "caption": "Liquidus surface in the CaO-MgO-SiO2 system as evaluated by Osborn, Muan [1]. Recent revisions concerning liquidus relations in the vicinity of the CaO·SiO2-MgO·SiO2 section reported by Kushiro [2], Longhi, Boudreau [3] and Liu, Presnall [4] are also incorporated in the figure. Legend: MS based solution phases - protoenstatite (Pen), orthoenstatite (Oen), pigeonite (Pi). References (printed p. 135): [1] E. F. Osborn, A. Muan, Ceramic Foundation 1960, Columbus/Ohio; [2] I. Kushiro, Am. Mineral. 57 (1972) 1260/71; [3] J. Longhi, A. E. Boudreau, Am. Mineral. 65 (1980) 563/73; [4] T.-C. Liu, D. C. Presnall, Am. Mineral. 74 (1989) 1032/7; [5] H. C. Lin, W. R. Foster, J. Am. Ceram. Soc. 58 (1975) 73; [6] W. Gutt, Nature 207 (1965) 184/5; [7] C. M. Schlaudt, D. M. Roy, J. Am. Ceram. Soc. 49 (1966) 430/2; [8] D. Mosley, F. P. Glasser, J. Mat. Sci. 17 (1982) 2736/40; [9] W. D. Carlson, Am. Mineral. 73 (1988) 232/41."
  },
  "digitization": {
    "render": "pdfPage 154 at 400 dpi (3306 × 4673 px); pixel = full-page coordinates",
