    "warpCorrection": {
      "reason": "With the corners alone the compound circles are displaced up to 13 px (≈0.8 wt%), smoothly across the page (scan warp).",
      "model": "Quadratic map page pixel → ideal pixel, fitted to the 3 corner circles (weight 10) and 10 compound circles (CS, C3S2, C2S, C3S, MS, M2S, CMS2, C2MS2, CMS, C3MS2). Features f = [1, x, y, x², xy, y²] with x = (px − 1100)/1000, y = (py − 1100)/1000; ideal = f · C, then wt% from the corner triangle.",
      "C": [[1096.487, 1090.701], [988.162, -13.506], [-7.08, 987.931], [12.132, 19.183], [11.607, 12.475], [0.407, 6.509]],
      "residuals": "≤ 4.5 px (≈0.25 wt%) at the circles; leave-one-out ≤ 7 px (≈0.4 wt%)."
    },
    "method": "Boundary curves isolated by stroke width; junctions from intersections of line fits to the strokes around each point (directions given where labels or curvature disturb the fit); saddle points = boundary × compound join (drawn compound circles); edge points = line fit of the boundary end × triangle edge."
  },
