    "notes": "Each triangle has exactly one liquidus invariant below. Fig. 3.250 draws solid solutions with tie-line fans: wollastonite ss towards CMS2, pyroxene ss CMS2–MS, monticellite–forsterite ss; modelled at stoichiometry. Inset 'T < 1372 °C': below 1372 °C the bredigite solution phase (7CaO·MgO·4SiO2 – 5CaO·MgO·3SiO2, Lin, Foster [5]) appears on the C2S–C3MS2 line; sub-solidus only, not modelled."
  },
